{
  "about": "Each market's strategies for the daily scan (tools/scan/strategies.py). 'live' makes the orders the bridge places; each of 'shadows' runs on the same data every day, its orders kept in the private store and never placed, its results tracked on the page beside the live one's. A strategy: name (lowercase, digits, -), env (the model's research switches, X_*), optional ref (a git commit or tag: the model built at that version), optional only (\"aim\": the UK's AIM shares only, which pay no stamp duty), optional app (\"single\": the single-share model, apps/ofm_single, every share learnt and backtested on its own bars only; shadows only). Changing a market's strategy is a change to this file, reviewed in a pull request. A market's budget ({\"total\": T, \"slots\": [k, ...]}) runs the live strategy once for each number of trades k, T/k each, and trades the k whose year before was best, chosen day by day (tools/scan/strategies.py).",
